.TH BUFFER_CHUNKED 3
.SH NAME
buffer_chunked \- decode the chunked transfer encoding of a buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "int buffer_chunked(buffer* " b ", buffer* " other ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR buffer_chunked ()
initializes
.I b
as a buffer that reads the data of the chunked transfer encoding (RFC 9112) found in
.IR other .
Chunk sizes, chunk extensions, line ends and trailers are removed. At the last chunk
.I b
reads the end of the file and the bytes behind the trailers stay in
.IR other ,
so a keep-alive connection can go on. An input that stops in the middle of a chunk is an
error (errno EPIPE), not an end of file; a damaged size gives EINVAL.
.P
.BR buffer_close (3)
on
.I b
frees it and leaves
.I other
open.
.P
This works on a plain
.B buffer
and blocks as the buffer does; for non-blocking connections use
.BR http_recv (3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
1 on success, 0 if the memory is short.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
buffer dec;
char tmp[512];
ssize_t n;

buffer_chunked(&dec, &in);
while((n = buffer_get(&dec, tmp, sizeof(tmp))) > 0)
  buffer_put(buffer_1, tmp, n);
buffer_close(&dec);
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
buffer_chunked_encode(3), http_recv(3)
